$image_face_swap — Flux.2 Klein face/head swap

SUMMARY
  Swaps a donor face onto target image(s) using Flux.2 Klein 9B FP8 multi-reference
  edit (comfy_lib in-process). Derived from
  comfy_workflows/Flux 2 Klein Precise Face_Head Swap Final V2.json.

SYNTAX
  $image_face_swap
  $image_face_swap[3]
  $image_face_swap(steps=20, cfg=4.0, seed=42)
  $image_face_swap(model='klein-fp8')

INPUT
  images[]  — target photo(s) to edit (must NOT be labeled 'face')
  labels[]  — one image labeled 'face' (donor face via $add_label('face'))
  prompts[] — optional; overrides default swap instruction

OUTPUT
  images[] — one swapped PNG per (target, face) job; repeat adds variants

BUNDLE LAYOUT
  @target: $file('body.png')
  @donor:  $file('face.png') -> $add_label('face')
  @target -> @donor -> $image_face_swap

  Target = images[] entry not tagged face.
  Donor  = images[] entry labeled face.

DEFAULT PROMPT
  English instruction from the Comfy workflow (two-reference Klein edit).
  Override with prompts[] or prompt=.

ARGUMENTS
  model=   — Klein checkpoint alias (default klein-fp8 → flux2Klein9bFp8_fp8)
  prompt=  — override default swap instruction
  width= / height= — output size (default: target image size, snapped to 16px)
  steps=   — diffusion steps (default 20 for FP8 base)
  cfg=     — classifier-free guidance (default 4.0)
  seed=    — fixed seed; with repeat, seed+0..n-1 per variant
  gpu=     — use CUDA when true (default true)
  [n]      — repeat variants per job (encode once, n samples)

MODELS
  models/flux2klein/flux2Klein9bFp8_fp8.safetensors
  models/text_encoders/qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors
  models/vae/flux2-vae.safetensors

DEPENDENCIES
  .venvs/media (comfy-kitchen for FP8; tools/setup_external_venvs.ps1)

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EXTERNAL_VENV_image_face_swap=.venvs/media
  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE_FACE_SWAP=1 — placeholder PNGs, no model load

EXAMPLE
  @body: $file('portrait.png')
  @face_src: $file('donor_face.png') -> $add_label('face')
  @body -> @face_src -> $image_face_swap

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared; images[] replaced with outputs.
